        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(skill-workshop): add restore action for quarantined proposals and display scan findings",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nQuarantined skill workshop proposals were a dead end: users could not see scan findings, could not restore them to pending, and had no path forward in the UI. The only workaround was manually editing `proposal.json`.\n\nFixes #106134\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThree concrete problems addressed:\n\n1. **Scan findings invisible**: `SkillWorkshopProposal` type dropped `scan` and `statusReason` fields. Now they're displayed in the UI for quarantined proposals.\n2. **No restore action**: Backend `withPendingSkillProposalMutation` gates all mutations on `status === \"pending\"`, so quarantined proposals had zero available operations.\n3. **No restore button**: UI only rendered action buttons for pending proposals.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Quarantined proposals now show scan findings (severity badges, file:line, rule message) in the detail card\n- New \"Restore\" button moves quarantined proposals back to pending state\n- Restore re-scans content for fresh security assessment (consistent with apply behavior)\n- Restored proposals can then be revised and re-applied\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [x] All 36 workshop service tests pass (including 2 new restore tests)\n- [x] `npx oxfmt --check` passes on all changed files\n- Changed files: `src/skills/workshop/`, `src/gateway/server-methods/skills.ts`, `ui/src/lib/skill-workshop/`, `ui/src/pages/skill-workshop/`, `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
